WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.870
We went to bed about 11 o’clock.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:12.390
Just at daybreak, I was awakened by a series of terrible screams from Bill.

3
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:18.850
Red Chief was sitting on Bill’s chest, with one hand holding his hair.

4
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.030
In the other, he had a sharp knife.

5
00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:29.470
He was attempting to cut off the top of Bill’s head, based on what he had declared the night before.

6
00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.860
I got the knife away from the boy.

7
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.660
But, after that event, Bill’s spirit was broken.

8
00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:47.200
He lay down, but he never closed an eye again in sleep as long as that boy was with us.

9
00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:54.660
“Do you think anybody will pay out money to get a little imp like that back home?” Bill asked.

10
00:00:55.370 --> 00:00:56.320
“Sure,” I said.

11
00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:00.140
“A boy like that is just the kind that parents love.

12
00:01:00.510 --> 00:01:09.400
Now, you and the Chief get up and make something to eat, while I go up on the top of this mountain and look around.”

13
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.450
I climbed to the top of the mountain.

14
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:20.230
Over toward Summit, I expected to see the men of the village searching the countryside.

15
00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:23.310
But all was peaceful.

16
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:35.790
“Perhaps,” says I to myself, “it has not yet been discovered that the wolves have taken the lamb from the fold.”

17
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.670
I went back down the mountain.

18
00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:48.010
When I got to the cave, I found Bill backed up against the side of it.

19
00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:54.050
He was breathing hard, with the boy threatening to strike him with a rock.

20
00:01:55.220 --> 00:02:01.610
“He put a red-hot potato down my back,” explained Bill, “and then crushed it with his foot.

21
00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.550
I hit his ears.

22
00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.250
Have you got a gun with you, Sam?”

23
00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:13.270
I took the rock away from the boy and ended the argument.

24
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.790
“I’ll fix you,” says the boy to Bill.

25
00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.270
“No man ever yet struck the Red Chief but what he got paid for it.

26
00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:23.790
You better be careful!”

27
00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:38.410
After eating, the boy takes a leather object with strings tied around it from his clothes and goes outside the cave unwinding it.

28
00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.930
Then we heard a kind of shout.

29
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:46.370
It was Red Chief holding a sling in one hand.

30
00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.750
He moved it faster and faster around his head.

31
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:59.050
Just then I heard a heavy sound and a deep breath from Bill.

32
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:07.310
A rock the size of an egg had hit him just behind his left ear.

33
00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:14.310
Bill fell in the fire across the frying pan of hot water for washing the dishes.

34
00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:21.570
I pulled him out and poured cold water on his head for half an hour.

35
00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:28.370
Then I went out and caught that boy and shook him.

36
00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:34.890
“If your behavior doesn’t improve,” says I, “I’ll take you straight home.

37
00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:38.290
Now, are you going to be good, or not?”

38
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.370
“I was only funning,” says he.

39
00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.770
“I didn’t mean to hurt Old Hank.

40
00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.690
But what did he hit me for?

41
00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.150
I’ll behave if you don’t send me home.”

42
00:03:50.600 --> 00:04:01.650
I thought it best to send a letter to old man Dorset that day, demanding the ransom and telling how it should be paid.

43
00:04:02.560 --> 00:04:03.730
The letter said:

44
00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:11.220
“We have your boy hidden in a place far from Summit.

45
00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:25.900
We demand $1,500 for his return; the money to be left at midnight tonight at the same place and in the same box as your answer.

46
00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:34.540
"If you agree to these terms, send the answer in writing by a messenger tonight at half past 8 o’clock.

47
00:04:36.450 --> 00:04:45.020
After crossing Owl Creek, on the road to Poplar Cove, there are three large trees.

48
00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:52.520
At the bottom of the fence, opposite the third tree, will be a small box.

49
00:04:53.370 --> 00:05:00.460
The messenger will place the answer in this box and return immediately to Summit.

50
00:05:01.850 --> 00:05:07.300
If you fail to agree to our demand, you will never see your boy again.

51
00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:19.740
If you pay the money as demanded, he will be returned to you safe and well within three hours.”

52
00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.740
I took the letter and walked over to Poplar Cove.

53
00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:31.680
I then sat around the post office and store.

54
00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:42.820
An old man there says he hears Summit is all worried because of Ebenezer Dorset’s boy having been lost or stolen.

55
00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:45.760
That was all I wanted to know.

56
00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.600
I mailed my letter and left.
